# NanoPi R2C (RK3328) router trim fragment on top of the R2C profile.
# Invariant: keep the router contract; disable only board-irrelevant surface.
#
# Keep: Ethernet+USB-NIC routing, nftables/iptables, WireGuard, IPv6, PPPoE,
# namespaces/cgroups/seccomp/BPF, Landlock, ext4/overlayfs, SD/MMC/eMMC,
# USB storage/UAS, RK3328 thermal/cpufreq, and the USB host path.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEVER disable these — required by fragment.r2c:
#   FTRACE, TRACING, FUNCTION_TRACER, TRACEPOINTS,
#   KPROBES, KPROBE_EVENTS, PERF_EVENTS,
#   SECURITY, SECURITYFS, SECURITY_LANDLOCK,
#   BPF, BPF_SYSCALL, BPF_JIT, BPF_LSM, BPF_EVENTS,
#   DEBUG_INFO_BTF, MOTORCOMM_PHY, USB_RTL8152, USB_USBNET,
#   PPP, PPPOE, IPV6_SEG6_LWTUNNEL, LSM, SMB_SERVER
# NEVER write =n for def_bool symbols:
#   IPV6_SEG6_BPF, GLOB (select'd by filesystems)
# NEVER write =n for ZRAM_BACKEND_LZ4 / CRYPTO_LZ4 — r2c sets them =y.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

